WEBVTT

00:00.880 --> 00:05.480
<i>Oh! You can definitely see what 
look like skeletons through the window!</i>

00:05.850 --> 00:10.360
<i>The smoke makes it hard to see, 
but there seem to be giant bones, as well.</i>

00:11.050 --> 00:13.890
<i>I'm glad that the children 
were saved in the end,</i>

00:13.890 --> 00:20.860
<i>but this program will tackle unlicensed 
childcare centers as a social issue.</i>

00:14.250 --> 00:17.990
Oh, wow! All this happened yesterday?!

00:17.990 --> 00:20.370
I guess ghosts <i>are</i> real!

00:21.510 --> 00:22.880
Looks like it.

00:26.850 --> 00:29.530
And they were a lot closer than I thought.

02:07.800 --> 02:09.290
Hey, Misaki.

02:09.880 --> 02:14.090
Doesn't it bother you, hanging out 
with the guy who killed you?

02:14.090 --> 02:16.940
Nope! I've never been killed before!

02:17.270 --> 02:21.070
It was super thrilling, so I don't mind!

02:21.470 --> 02:25.420
Oh, right. You've always had a screw loose.

02:26.200 --> 02:30.540
Anyway, I never knew Clarissa 
owned this building.

02:30.960 --> 02:31.770
Um...

02:33.350 --> 02:38.630
I'm sure this is inconvenient for you, 
but I really appreciate your help.

02:39.010 --> 02:42.860
To be frank, I know almost 
nothing about this world.

02:42.860 --> 02:44.760
Oh, well. That aside...

02:46.630 --> 02:48.600
Are you seriously going to live <i>here</i>?

02:48.870 --> 02:51.250
<b>The Torture Building</b>

02:48.870 --> 02:51.250
<b>The Torture Building</b>

02:50.830 --> 02:55.360
That body you, uh, reincarnated 
into has a family, right?

02:55.360 --> 02:56.620
What about them?

02:57.020 --> 03:00.900
Since it's currently "summer 
vacation," I told this body's—

03:00.900 --> 03:05.700
I told Polka Shinoyama's family that
 he's on a journey of self-discovery.

03:05.930 --> 03:06.910
I'm on a journey of self-discovery

03:07.190 --> 03:11.280
Clarissa suggested I periodically 
send them these postcards.

03:11.280 --> 03:14.170
That's a trick for covering 
up someone's time of death.

03:14.630 --> 03:20.630
But I don't know what I'll do after that.
 I only know his family's names.

03:20.630 --> 03:24.390
Can't you pull the memories 
out of his brain or something?

03:24.790 --> 03:29.440
Language was easy to retrieve because 
it was deeply ingrained via repetition,

03:29.440 --> 03:32.560
but the older the memory is, 
the harder it is to recover.

03:32.560 --> 03:33.810
Or, you could say...

03:35.540 --> 03:38.480
...his last memory left 
too strong an impression.

03:38.820 --> 03:40.880
Anyway, another world, huh?

03:41.200 --> 03:44.910
After seeing those monster skeletons, 
I've gotta believe it. But still...

03:44.910 --> 03:50.290
I'm still not certain this <i>is</i> another world. 
There are similarities.

03:50.290 --> 03:57.590
<b>Let's compare!! 
How big are whales?</b>

03:50.290 --> 03:57.590
<b>m 0 0 l 200 0 200 100 0 100</b>

03:50.290 --> 03:57.590
<b>Measuring and comparing whale sizes</b>

03:50.290 --> 03:57.590
<b> Large and small whales</b>

03:50.290 --> 03:57.590
<b>Whales, Mammals of the Sea</b>

03:50.720 --> 03:57.590
For example, your "whales" are written of 
in my world as legendary beasts.

03:57.910 --> 04:03.670
But what matters most to me is that the 
Geldwood religion doesn't exist here.

04:03.670 --> 04:05.510
The Geld... What now?

04:06.610 --> 04:10.050
They considered me an abomination 
and tried to destroy me.

04:10.520 --> 04:13.890
I was a colossal skeleton 
monster over there, you see.

04:13.890 --> 04:16.470
Oh, you mean that thing.

04:16.470 --> 04:18.610
What did they call you over there?

04:18.610 --> 04:23.670
Well, in you tongue,
 I was called the... Cadaver Spirit?

04:23.670 --> 04:28.450
No, the Corpse God.

04:28.450 --> 04:30.480
The Corpse God...

04:30.480 --> 04:31.850
That's so cool!

04:31.850 --> 04:34.160
Y-You think so?

04:34.160 --> 04:37.290
Peace may finally be within my grasp.

04:37.640 --> 04:43.280
All I need to do now is talk down 
whoever paid to have this body killed.

04:43.910 --> 04:47.170
I don't know who the client was,
 and neither does Misaki.

04:47.170 --> 04:49.360
Didn't you ask Clarissa?

04:49.360 --> 04:50.260
I did.

04:50.260 --> 04:54.410
She said she had to keep the secret,
but let me use this floor in exchange.

04:55.120 --> 05:00.610
Forcing her to speak is a last resort. 
I'll investigate on my own first.

05:00.610 --> 05:04.900
And Clarissa-san agreed not to accept 
any more contracts on my life.

05:04.900 --> 05:07.320
And you just <i>believed</i> her?

05:07.320 --> 05:11.460
Clarissa's not the only intermediary
 for assassins, you know?

05:11.460 --> 05:16.450
Well, it's not like many people 
could kill a freak like you.

05:16.450 --> 05:18.440
Except Lemmings, maybe.

05:19.360 --> 05:20.460
Lemmings?

05:20.720 --> 05:23.020
Oh, nothing. Forget about it.

05:23.020 --> 05:24.050
Anyway—

05:24.300 --> 05:26.810
Hey! This thing's so cool!

05:26.810 --> 05:29.930
How does it work?! Coin batteries?!

05:30.210 --> 05:34.020
Are you sure <i>you</i> don't mind having 
Misaki around? She did kill you.

05:34.340 --> 05:36.940
I mean, I wasn't the one who died.

05:41.050 --> 05:43.810
Was bringing this nutjob back 
to life really a good idea?

05:44.710 --> 05:50.450
Well, this body's owner, Polka-kun,
 told me to forgive her.

05:50.450 --> 05:51.700
So it should be fine.

05:51.700 --> 05:52.700
Huh?

05:53.260 --> 05:55.610
You've talked with Polka's ghost?

05:55.930 --> 05:59.050
More than that. He's right there.

05:59.050 --> 05:59.830
Hm?

05:59.830 --> 06:03.050
**0,000 yen

06:00.060 --> 06:03.050
That's the drone I lost control of yesterday!

06:03.300 --> 06:08.570
His soul was still in this body, 
so I imbued it into a nearby vessel.

06:08.890 --> 06:12.520
Do you mind if I borrow this until
 I find a substitute for him to possess?

06:13.230 --> 06:16.250
I don't, but forget that.

06:16.250 --> 06:19.640
You mean you just swap people's 
souls around, like doll clothes?

06:19.640 --> 06:24.190
I won't deny it. Human lives 
are like toys or dolls to me.

06:25.270 --> 06:27.240
<i>I knew this guy was bad news.</i>

06:28.160 --> 06:31.990
<i>Our lives really are just playthings to him.</i>

06:32.610 --> 06:35.090
<i>I've gotta keep my guard up.</i>

06:35.440 --> 06:40.810
Now, for the sake of my peaceful life,
 it's time to earn some money.

06:41.350 --> 06:44.210
Does this world have any jobs I'd be good at?

06:44.470 --> 06:46.710
How about murder? Or mugging?

06:46.950 --> 06:49.050
Assassination isn't my strong suit.

06:49.050 --> 06:52.790
You're good enough to kill me, 
so it should be a cinch.

06:52.790 --> 06:53.700
Fair point.

06:53.700 --> 06:55.030
Don't encourage her!

06:56.810 --> 06:59.940
Hang on, we've got a visitor. 
Probably for Misaki.

06:59.940 --> 07:01.650
Huh? For me?

07:02.910 --> 07:05.920
You're Assassin Zaki, right?

07:05.920 --> 07:09.660
Unless I do something, 
another gang's hitmen are gonna off me.

07:09.660 --> 07:11.240
Can you help me?

07:11.610 --> 07:15.580
I dunno. I'm in the middle of another job...

07:15.580 --> 07:17.880
Please! Without you, I'll—

07:17.880 --> 07:18.930
All right.

07:18.930 --> 07:19.620
Huh?!

07:20.470 --> 07:22.170
I accept your request.

07:22.170 --> 07:25.230
Hey, punk! Were you listening in on—

07:25.740 --> 07:29.090
Okay! If Polka-kun's on board,
 I'll take the job.

07:29.320 --> 07:30.100
Huh?!

07:31.830 --> 07:35.790
What the hell is he thinking?

07:40.350 --> 07:42.640
According to my info broker,

07:42.640 --> 07:44.880
they oughta be asleep in there.

07:44.880 --> 07:48.610
Those are some awfully careless hitmen.

07:48.610 --> 07:51.360
They worked with Jinba, a guy you offed.

07:51.360 --> 07:56.250
They're not so much assassins as psychos 
who murder their targets' whole families.

08:00.580 --> 08:02.500
That old guy's buddies, huh?

08:07.960 --> 08:09.460
An ambush?!

08:18.980 --> 08:20.010
Take that!

08:30.750 --> 08:34.310
Aww! For hitmen, these guys are real wimps!

08:35.740 --> 08:36.610
Huh?

08:39.340 --> 08:42.040
Well, that's 'cause we're not hitmen.

08:42.040 --> 08:46.630
But we'll still lose face if 
we don't get even for our boss.

08:46.630 --> 08:49.320
Hey, finish her off!

08:50.750 --> 08:53.400
Yes, I see. I understand.

08:53.400 --> 08:55.050
The hell are <i>you</i> doing here?!

08:55.340 --> 08:58.740
I accept your request, as well.

08:58.740 --> 09:00.730
Huh? You what?

09:00.730 --> 09:02.940
Screw it! You can die with Zaki!

09:04.690 --> 09:06.840
Oh, I forgot to mention.

09:07.270 --> 09:09.540
Misaki-chan is a zombie now,

09:10.070 --> 09:12.390
so she won't die from a few holes in her.

09:12.390 --> 09:13.280
Ooh!

09:13.500 --> 09:16.250
I'd say she's quite a 
bit tougher than before.

09:23.230 --> 09:25.430
Wh-What the hell are you?!

09:28.770 --> 09:30.130
<i>Can you hear me, Polka?</i>

09:30.410 --> 09:31.560
Um...

09:32.000 --> 09:35.110
"Speaking." Is that the right 
greeting in this situation?

09:35.110 --> 09:37.720
<i>Did you know this was a trap?</i>

09:38.590 --> 09:39.470
No.

09:40.020 --> 09:42.300
I merely accepted a request...

09:47.940 --> 09:51.400
...from the children whose ghosts haunt him.

09:57.780 --> 09:59.990
Oh, man! Oh, man!

10:00.700 --> 10:02.910
This is a blast!

10:03.180 --> 10:05.370
Wh-What the hell...?

10:05.810 --> 10:08.640
Let go! You stupid brats!

10:13.880 --> 10:19.800
I won't let them kill any more people. 
Not your mommies or daddies either.

10:20.120 --> 10:24.510
Mommy... Daddy...

10:26.550 --> 10:27.390
I'm sorry.

10:28.350 --> 10:32.630
This isn't a rescue.
 I'm doing it partly out of spite.

10:33.290 --> 10:36.600
So I won't demand payment for it.

10:39.850 --> 10:44.240
Wow! The bullet holes are better already!

10:44.240 --> 10:48.460
I guess I really am a monster now!

10:48.920 --> 10:51.250
But my instincts might not be quite as sharp.

10:51.250 --> 10:54.220
I mean, I've never gotten 
shot in the back before!

10:54.220 --> 10:57.280
Do all girls in this world 
undress so casually?

10:58.110 --> 10:59.460
Hey, Polka.

11:00.410 --> 11:04.010
Why'd you listen to those dead kids?

11:04.010 --> 11:06.890
I thought lives were toys to you.

11:07.210 --> 11:11.350
Yeah, every human life is 
ultimately someone's toy.

11:13.240 --> 11:18.970
But I like toys. 
They can make children smile.

11:23.980 --> 11:26.540
So of course I take good care of them.

11:27.210 --> 11:32.500
No way in hell will I abandon 
them to the vicissitudes of fate.

11:33.060 --> 11:34.880
<i>Oh, so that's it.</i>

11:35.470 --> 11:41.380
<i>The biggest difference in our values 
is how we see toys, not lives.</i>

11:41.850 --> 11:44.100
<i>No wonder we were talking past each other.</i>

11:44.730 --> 11:47.670
<i>Polka may be a dangerous guy...</i>

11:48.680 --> 11:51.610
Well, you'd better stay dead this time.

11:52.230 --> 11:56.650
Otherwise, us retrievers don't get paid.

11:58.460 --> 12:02.170
<i>...but me and Misaki are probably 
the real scumbags here.</i>

12:03.870 --> 12:06.570
Oh, sorry. I ought to watch my language.

12:07.580 --> 12:09.120
Being casual is fine.

12:10.050 --> 12:14.080
I mean, counting your past life, 
you've gotta be older than me.

12:17.540 --> 12:20.710
<i>So you see, it was a real hassle.</i>

12:20.710 --> 12:24.400
Yes. Thank you, Takumi-kun.

12:25.610 --> 12:30.020
What? Yes, I really did back out 
of the hit on Polka Shinoyama.

12:30.620 --> 12:34.460
I couldn't stand those 
stuck-up people anyway.

12:34.460 --> 12:37.370
The remnants you dealt with 
today shouldn't be an issue.

12:38.700 --> 12:41.940
It appears they've made 
a few too many enemies.

12:42.700 --> 12:46.410
Damn it! That freak is gonna pay for this!

12:46.410 --> 12:49.370
Bring out the whole armory!

12:51.050 --> 12:53.620
Wh-What happened here?

12:53.620 --> 12:56.840
Don't tell me that freak did this, too...

12:58.660 --> 13:02.550
H-Hey! This ain't the time for jokes!

13:03.410 --> 13:07.070
L-Lemmings...

13:07.550 --> 13:09.970
You've gotta be kidding! That's...

13:10.210 --> 13:12.810
That's just a tall tale!

13:14.310 --> 13:18.000
<b>Mummy</b>

13:14.680 --> 13:18.810
So, vampires are only legends in this world?

13:16.370 --> 13:18.810
<b>Vampire</b>

13:18.810 --> 13:21.300
Wait, they were real in yours?!

13:21.300 --> 13:24.780
Lucky! Vampires are so cool.

13:24.780 --> 13:29.330
With enough mana, I might eventually 
be able to evolve you into one.

13:29.330 --> 13:30.280
For real?!

13:30.740 --> 13:34.330
What, like changing classes? 
This is straight out of a video game.

13:34.720 --> 13:39.210
<i>No idea how long this monster and 
zombie will keep playing house.</i>

13:40.040 --> 13:43.550
<i>Well, I can play along for 
a little while longer.</i>

13:43.550 --> 13:46.870
<i>I was getting bored of my life, anyway.</i>

13:56.300 --> 13:58.900
Are you sure about this, Clarissa?

13:59.190 --> 14:01.980
About what? Polka-kun?

14:01.980 --> 14:05.940
So you're close enough to 
casually call him -kun?

14:06.690 --> 14:09.030
He's got a soft spot for children.

14:09.030 --> 14:12.160
A weakness like that makes
 him easy to control.

14:12.160 --> 14:15.590
<i>Clarissa's got a spot for kids, too,
 if you ask me.</i>

14:17.970 --> 14:21.270
Clarissa, phone call for you.

14:23.020 --> 14:24.250
It's me.

14:25.440 --> 14:29.470
How tedious. We went over all that yesterday.

14:31.250 --> 14:34.550
"Polka Shinoyama is just a high schooler"?

14:34.550 --> 14:37.640
Be serious. I believed 
you when you said that,

14:37.640 --> 14:40.010
and now one of our stars is a corpse.

14:40.910 --> 14:44.400
Consider our relationship 
on hold for a while.

14:46.900 --> 14:50.490
<i>Wasn't</i> Polka Shinoyama just 
a high schooler, though?

14:50.490 --> 14:52.360
At least until he died?

14:52.980 --> 14:55.850
I wouldn't be so sure about that.

14:57.800 --> 15:02.250
But we got rid of one unpleasant client,
 and that's what counts.

15:03.000 --> 15:04.960
Now, shall we celebrate?

15:07.280 --> 15:10.590
For the first time in ages, 
this town might just charm me.

15:14.730 --> 15:19.240
Choose your dance partners 
with care, Polka-kun.

15:21.940 --> 15:26.690
P-Please. Can't you see I'm begging you here?

15:26.910 --> 15:29.320
I really can't pay.

15:29.320 --> 15:33.980
I had no idea one beer cost 60,000 yen.

15:35.700 --> 15:40.160
Hey, is it just me, or are more bars 
ripping people off than ever?

15:40.160 --> 15:44.090
Yes, I hear there's one on the fourth 
floor of the building next door.

15:44.090 --> 15:50.170
Huh. Well, a good drink in 
this place ain't cheap either.

15:52.700 --> 15:54.590
Anyway, where's Clarissa-chan?!

15:54.590 --> 15:58.040
She's on the late shift today. 
She'll start at midnight.

15:58.040 --> 16:00.600
Seriously? That's not her regular time.

16:00.600 --> 16:01.810
Urgent business?

16:01.810 --> 16:04.690
Or has something been going on lately?

16:06.240 --> 16:09.630
Oh, no. I don't think there's 
been anything unusual.

16:09.630 --> 16:11.030
Yeah?

16:11.410 --> 16:13.760
What about the Shakuzawa 
Building fire yesterday?

16:13.760 --> 16:18.570
My coworkers were talking about people 
seeing skeletons in there. Skeletons!

16:18.990 --> 16:21.250
But what's so scary about that?!

16:21.250 --> 16:23.410
Once we're dead, we'll <i>all</i> be skeletons!

16:23.410 --> 16:26.540
Don't forget corpse wax and mummies.

16:26.860 --> 16:30.170
Zombies are more my speed.

16:30.420 --> 16:33.220
Watch out, or I'll feast on your flesh!

16:34.340 --> 16:38.810
Exterminate zombie. Crush head.

16:39.700 --> 16:42.650
We have a "hands off" policy.

16:45.540 --> 16:47.730
Man. Zombies, huh?

16:48.020 --> 16:52.990
What'll happen to Misaki's body? 
It hasn't been long since she got shot.

16:53.370 --> 16:58.200
Her body self-repairs and resists
 putrefaction, so she'll be fine.

16:58.750 --> 17:03.910
But she might be a bit stronger 
and less sensitive than before.

17:03.910 --> 17:06.710
She should eat raw meat if 
she gets seriously injured.

17:06.710 --> 17:11.020
Like one of those "carnivorous women"? 
Wow! That's so cool!

17:11.020 --> 17:12.700
I'm not so sure.

17:12.700 --> 17:16.510
Also, your saliva should have 
a strong paralytic effect.

17:16.510 --> 17:17.330
Huh?

17:18.620 --> 17:22.100
Oh! I think my spit tastes 
sweeter than usual!

17:22.310 --> 17:25.120
Anyone you bite will be 
paralyzed for a little whi—

17:25.370 --> 17:26.310
Slide

17:26.580 --> 17:27.540
<b>Thud</b>

17:26.900 --> 17:28.760
Polka?!

17:28.760 --> 17:29.520
It's true!

17:29.520 --> 17:30.790
What's wrong with you?!

17:31.630 --> 17:33.750
Want me to bite you, too, Kurupon?

17:33.750 --> 17:37.570
A nibble from a girl's basically a kiss,
 you know? Lucky you.

17:37.570 --> 17:38.620
Quiet, 3-D!

17:38.620 --> 17:40.240
Three-D?!

17:40.240 --> 17:44.240
Some women assume every man sees 
a kiss from them as a prize.

17:44.240 --> 17:45.960
To such self-obsessed women,

17:46.170 --> 17:48.370
my answer will forever be a staunch "no"!

17:48.640 --> 17:53.290
They're as bad as men who offer to make 
a stranger "their woman" as a reward!

17:53.290 --> 17:54.300
Kurupon!

17:54.300 --> 17:57.120
You're a monster created by modern society!

17:57.120 --> 17:58.260
A monster!

17:58.990 --> 18:00.320
<i>Monster...</i>

18:00.680 --> 18:01.880
<i>That reminds me.</i>

18:01.880 --> 18:08.690
<i>Does this world have any superhuman 
bogeymen like the Calamity Crusher?</i>

18:10.370 --> 18:12.600
Do you think there really were gunshots?

18:12.600 --> 18:13.690
Beats me.

18:14.010 --> 18:16.960
But someone called it in, so we have to check.

18:26.900 --> 18:28.040
What was that sound?

18:41.850 --> 18:42.540
Huh?

18:42.540 --> 18:44.220
What happened here?!

18:44.810 --> 18:48.890
Come on, say something already.

18:49.380 --> 18:53.480
I'm bowing my head and apologizing, aren't I?

18:53.480 --> 18:54.570
Well?!

19:10.260 --> 19:11.490
Oh, damn it.

19:12.030 --> 19:14.860
I was so close to getting 
to see Clarissa-chan.

19:16.840 --> 19:19.570
This really blows.

19:22.050 --> 19:25.710
Oh, I was thinking. Your world uses 
the decimal system, too, right?

19:25.710 --> 19:26.720
That's right.

19:27.680 --> 19:30.460
I'm guessing people there 
have ten fingers, then?

19:30.460 --> 19:31.600
Ten fingers?

19:32.020 --> 19:35.140
Well, most do. Although 
there's some variation.

19:35.140 --> 19:40.430
Ten fingers leading to the decimal 
system is just one theory, you know?

19:40.430 --> 19:42.060
I'm surprised you know that.

19:42.440 --> 19:46.160
Wait, could people from different 
worlds really look that alike?

19:46.590 --> 19:50.640
And would magic from another 
world work the same way here?

19:50.640 --> 19:51.740
You have a point.

19:58.460 --> 20:03.420
My world and this one may 
be connected somehow.

20:03.850 --> 20:07.220
Too much wouldn't make sense otherwise.

20:07.680 --> 20:09.590
Paralysis finally wore off?

20:09.590 --> 20:10.520
Yeah.

20:10.830 --> 20:13.600
I'll have to add biting to my bag of tricks!

20:13.600 --> 20:15.470
Wouldn't punching be faster?

20:15.470 --> 20:18.090
I can use it to immobilize people!

20:18.090 --> 20:23.080
I used to nail gun them to the floor,
 but now I can save on nails!

20:23.080 --> 20:25.570
Yeah, that'll be better for the environment.

20:25.570 --> 20:30.460
Yes. The more ways you can 
incapacitate someone, the better.

20:31.730 --> 20:34.780
I'm guessing you've got 
a ton of tricks for that.

20:34.780 --> 20:37.820
You put those punks six feet under.

20:37.820 --> 20:39.990
Convenient that it hid the corpses, too.

20:39.990 --> 20:42.170
What? They're still alive.

20:42.170 --> 20:42.910
Huh?

20:44.010 --> 20:48.550
Though I doubt they're still sane, 
so they probably can't testify.

20:48.550 --> 20:49.810
"Probably" won't cut it!

20:49.810 --> 20:54.890
Don't worry. I made sure they'll 
never be able to kill anyone again.

20:59.170 --> 21:01.900
You reek of booze, Iwa-san.

21:02.260 --> 21:06.860
Better than the blood I smell on you.
 How'd that happen?

21:06.860 --> 21:09.830
It was self-defense. 
Even though I apologized,

21:09.830 --> 21:11.750
I thought they were going to kill me.

21:11.750 --> 21:13.960
Kill <i>you</i>? Gimme a break.

21:15.770 --> 21:19.350
So, what's this?

21:19.350 --> 21:21.090
I see.

21:21.090 --> 21:24.050
Well, now. So that's what this is about.

21:24.810 --> 21:28.690
I've never seen a human square knot before.

21:28.690 --> 21:32.470
No wonder the MIU called us in before 
starting their initial investigation.

21:32.970 --> 21:36.060
You think this is one of ours too?

21:36.060 --> 21:40.140
No other department knows what to 
do with borderline-occult stuff.

21:40.740 --> 21:43.690
Then it really must be our job.

21:43.690 --> 21:45.400
<b><Lemmings></b>

21:44.120 --> 21:48.660
Lemmings, the Grim Reaper, 
and the Fire-Breathing Bug.

21:45.400 --> 21:46.920
<b><Grim Reaper></b>

21:46.920 --> 21:48.660
<b><Fire-Breathing Bug></b>

21:49.870 --> 21:52.740
This might be our first 
troublemaker since them.

21:53.580 --> 21:55.540
I can hardly wait.

